WEBVTT

00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:02.216
One of the first public companies.

00:00:02.226 --> 00:00:05.325
In 1602, the Dutch East India Company

00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:08.019
sold shares to the public, with a

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:10.977
21-year monopoly on trade in Asia.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.207
Any citizen of the Dutch Republic could

00:00:13.217 --> 00:00:16.073
buy in, and over a thousand did.

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:18.322
And it was no ordinary company:

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:20.544
it could make treaties and wage war.

00:00:20.554 --> 00:00:22.989
Its spice trade made it a giant:

00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:25.398
nearly 5,000 voyages to Asia.

00:00:25.541 --> 00:00:26.976
So how did it end?

00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:30.256
Bankrupt by the late 1700s, the state

00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:32.989
dissolved it on the last day of

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:33.587
1799.
